      what:'The priest, in a cope, walks through the church sprinkling the people with holy water while the choir sings “Thou shalt sprinkle me, O Lord, with hyssop, and I shall be cleansed.” In Eastertide it is the Vidi aquam: “I saw water flowing from the temple.” Bless yourself as the water reaches you.',
